{"name":"Redbud","hex":"#ad5e65","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"redbud","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of several small trees, of the genus Cercis, having purple-pink flowers that appear before the leaves; the Judas tree."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/redbud"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cercis","blocks":[{"text":"Cercis is a genus of flowering plants in the subfamily Cercidoideae of the pea family Fabaceae. It contains small deciduous trees or large shrubs commonly known for the Judas tree in Europe or as redbuds in the USA. They are characterised by simple, rounded to heart-shaped leaves and pinkish-red flowers borne in the early spring on bare leafless shoots, on both branches and trunk (\"cauliflory\"). The genus contains ten species, native to warm temperate regions of North America, southern Europe, western and central Asia, and China."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Red_bud_2009.jpg/330px-Red_bud_2009.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cercis"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Redbud_in_Seven_Springs.JPG/500px-Redbud_in_Seven_Springs.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Redbud_in_Seven_Springs.JPG/1280px-Redbud_in_Seven_Springs.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Redbud_in_Seven_Springs.JPG/500px-Redbud_in_Seven_Springs.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARedbud_in_Seven_Springs.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/Cercis_canadensis_BW-03080-81.jpg/500px-Cercis_canadensis_BW-03080-81.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm